---
{
  "title": "Instagram messages and leads agent (simulation)",
  "summary": "How an agent sorts incoming messages, drafts replies and hands qualified contacts to a person.",
  "seoTitle": "Demo: an agent for Instagram leads",
  "description": "An interactive simulation with synthetic data: an agent sorts messages and comments, scores contacts and drafts replies that a person approves.",
  "kind": "demo",
  "status": "live",
  "draft": false,
  "clientConsent": false,
  "sector": "Marketing and sales",
  "stack": ["TypeScript", "Next.js"],
  "service": "ai-agents"
}
---

## What it shows

A simulation of the inbox and comments of a fictional business profile. The agent sorts each message (information request, sales interest, support, spam), scores the contacts and drafts a reply.

## Where a person steps in

Replies do not go out on their own: the draft is shown and approved by a person, and qualified contacts move on to the next step. The demo always shows what the agent decided and why.

## How it works in practice

An agent like this works through Instagram's official APIs for business accounts, within the platform's terms. The demo uses only synthetic profiles and messages: no real account is connected and no personal data is processed. Here the classifications are computed with fixed rules, not by an AI model: a real agent would use a language model, with the same approval step.
</file>

